A vote of confidence in British business, GSK's investment in Cambridge research center and potential future mergers.

• GSK invests £400m in research and development center in Cambridge to boost R&D efforts (source: <a href="https://www.theverge.com/2018/7/9/18556370/gsk-british-business-cambridge-research-center">The Verge</a>);
• GSK believes it can meet 20 potential medicines into late-stage trials this year (source: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/news/blogs/insider-news">The Guardian</a>), outpacing its competitors;
• The company is investing in a cancer specialist, Nuvalent, to cut costs and focus on prioritizing drugs.

articles.content_text:
This project parses JSON entirely on the GPU via wgpu compute shaders. The parser decomposes JSON parsing into a pipeline of parallel prefix scans, producing a flat tape of structural characters
This is purely for research into reducing JSON parsing into what Raph Levien calls invitingly parallel problems
Usage
fn main() {
    let json = r#"
    {
        "foo": "bar",
        "baz": {
            "wef": [1, 2, 3],
            "yearn": {
                "1": 2,
                "2": 3.0 
            } 
        } 
    }
    "#;

    let parser = slurpjson::Parser::try_new()?;
    let tape = parser.parse_str(&json)?;

    let document = slurpjson::Document::new(json.as_bytes(), &tape);

    dbg!(document);
}
